  "enhanced_information": "Thymidine kinase-deficient varicella-zoster virus (VZV) strains are resistant to acyclovir, making it ineffective for treating infections caused by this strain. Famciclovir, which is a prodrug that converts to an active form effective against VZV, is a suitable alternative and is supported by evidence indicating its efficacy against Human herpesvirus 3 (VZV). Ganciclovir is primarily used for cytomegalovirus (CMV) and is not effective for VZV, while cidofovir has limited efficacy against VZV and is not the first choice. Amantadine is not effective for VZV infections. Therefore, famciclovir is the best antiviral agent for treating shingles in this population."
